    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #319\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-83-implementation-audit-fixes-04-23-reject-thr_gczr63vyv2` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #83: item and relation mutations are now rejected once their database is archived.\n\n- Introduced one reusable guard in the choke-point data layer (`backend/packages/data/src/chokePoint/chokePoint.ts`) that returns a canonical `403 database_archived` instead of the previous generic `400 validation_failed`.\n- Applied it to every item mutation (create, property patch, soft delete, restore) and to both sides of relation create/update/delete.\n- Item creation carries the one explicit exception the issue calls for: a replay of an idempotency key that already committed a row before archival returns that existing row with no write and no side effects; a new key, or a key reservation whose row is missing, still gets `database_archived`.\n- Reads and restoring the database itself remain unaffected, as required.\n- Extended `backend/packages/data/src/chokePoint/itemsStore.ts` with a read-only `findIdempotentReplay` helper backing that carve-out.\n- Updated/added tests in `backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/chokePoint.test.ts` covering archived create/update, soft-delete/restore, relation mutations from either side, and the idempotent-replay-vs-new-key behavior.\n\nVerified with a fresh `pnpm install` in `backend`: unit tests (83/83), integration tests across all packages/modules/services (406/406), e2e tests (5/5), the dependency-boundaries check, and a full workspace TypeScript build all pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
